      {
        "position": 2,
        "title": "Dog bath massager with automatic soap dispenser",
        "text": "Dog bath massager with automatic soap dispenser is amazing. I have a husky with a lot of hair and this was so much easier than a typical bath. You can hold your dog with one hand and soap up with the other.",
        "rating": 5,
        "date": "May 30, 2025",
        "author": "K. Smith",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AFY7HE74IJXD726UFNPJWCEWYMCQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png"
      },
      {
        "position": 3,
        "title": "Bubblicious!",
        "text": "This thing is pretty cool, and has certainly upgraded bath time for my pits. It lathers and cleans their fur extremely well, and while it took them a little getting used to, they ended up liking the scrubbing vibrations. This has completely cut this routine down by half - I love it!",
        "rating": 4,
        "date": "July 20, 2025",
        "author": "IA",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AET3PMEXWGLWWOQB3NLCISQB6NGQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png"
      },
      {
        "position": 4,
        "title": "Cheaply made",
        "text": "We have three dogs, so I thought this would make it easier to bathe them. Don't use too thick of dog shampoo, or it won't work. When I went to tighten the container that holds the shampoo, the plastic handle started to separate. Cheaply made, and not very durable. I don't see this lasting very long. It is rechargeable, which is very nice. It's kinda bulky, but I will say once you get it working correctly, it does make it easier to wash your dogs.",
        "rating": 3,
        "date": "June 5, 2025",
        "author": "Shanody",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AE3XT7CXA67CEHAIZRCYYHUCINIQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png"
      },
      {
        "position": 5,
        "title": "Interesting idea…",
        "text": "We're in the middle of a home renovation and I put a dog bath in my laundry room. We have a 55-lb Lab and a 75 lb Lab mix. And they both get really, really dirty.I think this product is a good idea, but it's just not \"it\" for me. First of all, the Lab mix has thick fur (he's mixed with husky and Great Pyr) and a lot of body real estate and it's too annoying to have to keep opening and refilling. Plus, it's heavy even without water in it, and kind of loud.I appreciate the idea of mixing water and shampoo to create a lather because it can be hard to get the water to penetrate both dogs' fur and get a good lather going down to their skin. And while these products helped with that aspect of bathing, it made it difficult in other ways, so kind of a \"wash.\"",
        "rating": 4,
        "date": "June 3, 2025",
        "author": "DL",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AHV7HDLL3ADJQSMMCQPEX5JDIUVQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png"
      },
      {
        "position": 6,
        "title": "Fun idea",
        "text": "This is functional and pretty easy to use. It is a bit expensive for the quality, not sure how durable it will be in the long run. It's not super solid and it is a bit heavy for one hand and handling the dog at the same time. The idea is great but it could be better overall.",
