        "title": "Great Concept, Best for Small Dog",
        "text": "I was really excited to try this dog wash tool on our two pups! It arrived without instructions, but thankfully it’s pretty self-explanatory. The only hiccup was accessing the charging port—it was a bit tricky getting the rubber cover off, but with a little patience we managed to get it charging. The massager was made of a very soft material and the item is super simple to put together and clean up after use.We tested it first on our short-haired dog, and while it did a decent job cleaning him up, we quickly realized this product is definitely best suited for small dogs. It created a lot of suds but the water ran out very quickly, and there just wasn’t enough power or capacity to attempt washing our husky. We didn’t even try with him, knowing it wouldn’t be effective.So, if you have a small dog (think Chihuahua or anything in the 10–20 lb range), this could be a convenient option for quick washes or travel use. For medium to large dogs, though, it’s likely not going to be sufficient. Overall, a neat idea with some potential—but best for the little ones!",
